#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:2
msgid "Language contributor checklist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:5
msgid "1. Know that you are creating a 3rd party grammar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:7
msgid ""
"*Sadly, due to lack of maintainer time we no longer merge new languages "
"grammars into the core library.* Instead, the project works by encouraging "
"3rd party language grammar development by willing contributors ready to help "
"and maintain them. We're also happy to host those 3rd party language "
"grammars at the ``highlightjs`` GitHub organization. Or you're welcome to "
"host yourself - we're always happy to link to to new language grammars."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:14
msgid ""
"We also make it easy to build, maintain, and distribute 3rd party grammar "
"modules so that Highlight.js can always be easily extended with new "
"languages. Using a 3rd party language (for end users) is often as simple as "
"just adding a single line of code to their JavaScript or build system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:19
msgid ""
"We'd love to have your grammar as a 3rd party language module if you'd be "
"willing to maintain it over time.  It's easy to develop and publish a 3rd "
"party language module.  If you already started work in the main source tree "
"- it's trivial to convert your existing work into a 3rd party module. (you "
"pretty much just move your files into a new project folder)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:27
msgid "2. Read extra/3RD_PARTY_QUICK_START.md"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:29
msgid ""
"Next, read ``extra/3RD_PARTY_QUICK_START.md``.  This should provide you with "
"a very high-level overview of the steps for creating a third-party language "
"grammar for Highlight.js."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:35
msgid "3. Create a language grammar definition file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:37
msgid ""
"The file defines a function accepting a reference to the library and "
"returning a language object. The library parameter (``hljs``) is useful to "
"access common modes and regexps. You should not immediately call this "
"function (you only need to export it). Calling it is handled by the build "
"process and details differ for different build targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:44
msgid ""
"export default function(hljs) {\n"
"  return {\n"
"    name: \"Language Name\",\n"
"    keywords: 'foo bar',\n"
"    contains: [ ..., hljs.NUMBER_MODE, ... ]\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:52
msgid ""
"The name of the file is used as a short language identifier and should be "
"usable as a class name in HTML and CSS.  Typically you'll place this file in "
"your new grammar repository under ``my_new_grammar/src/languages/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:58
msgid "4. Add language metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:60
msgid ""
"At the top of the file there is a specially formatted comment with meta data "
"processed by a build system. Meta data format is simply key-value pairs each "
"occupying its own line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:65
msgid ""
"/*\n"
"Language: Superlanguage\n"
"Requires: java.js, sql.js\n"
"Author: John Smith <email@domain.com>\n"
"Contributors: Mike Johnson <...@...>, Matt Wilson <...@...>\n"
"Description: Some cool language definition\n"
"Website: https://superlanguage.example.com\n"
"*/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:74
msgid ""
"``Language`` — the only required header giving a human-readable language "
"name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:76
msgid ""
"``Requires`` — a list of other language files required for this language to "
"work. This make it possible to describe languages that extend definitions of "
"other ones. Required files aren't processed in any special way. The build "
"system just makes sure that they will be in the final package in "
"``LANGUAGES`` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:82
msgid "The meaning of the other headers should be pretty obvious."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:86
msgid "5. Create a code example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:88
msgid ""
"The code example is used both to test language detection and for the demo "
"page on https://highlightjs.org/. Put it in ``test/detect/<language>/default."
"txt``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:91
msgid ""
"Take inspiration from other languages in ``test/detect/`` and read :ref:"
"`testing instructions <basic-testing>` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:96
msgid "6. Write a class reference if your class uses custom classes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:98
msgid ""
"A class reference document should typically be placed at the root of your "
"language repository: ``css-class-reference.md``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:101
msgid ""
"Describe shortly names of all meaningful modes used in your language "
"definition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:103
msgid ""
"Note: If you use custom classes please be aware that all the build-in themes "
"are not going to support your custom classes and you should likely also "
"distribute your own custom theme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:109
msgid "7. Request a repository at the ``highlightjs`` organization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:111
msgid ""
"*This is optional.* Of course you are free to host your repository anywhere "
"you would like."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:114
msgid ""
"Request a new 3rd party grammar repository hosted in highlightjs with Issue "
"Type `**Issue: Request a new 3rd party grammar repository** <https://github."
"com/highlightjs/highlight.js/issues/new/choose>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:119
msgid "8. Create a pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../language-contribution.rst:121
msgid ""
"Submit a PR to add your language to `SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES.md <https://github."
"com/highlightjs/highlight.js/blob/main/SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES.md>`_."
msgstr ""
